## unknown_code
error[Z0401]: no warning has the code `W9999`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | warn("x", code: W9999)
  | ^^^^ not a code Zeff raises
  |
  = help: copy the code from the warning itself; `zeff help W0203` explains a code

## error_code
error[Z0401]: `code` of `warn` must be a warning's code, but this is `Z0101`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:17
  |
1 | warn("x", code: Z0101)
  |                 ^^^^^ an error's code
  |
  = help: a warning's code is `W` and four digits, as in `code: W0205`; `zeff help W0205` explains a code

## not_a_code
error[Z0401]: `code` of `note` must be a warning's code, but this is `skipped`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:17
  |
1 | note("x", code: "skipped")
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^ not a warning's code
  |
  = help: a warning's code is `W` and four digits, as in `code: W0205`; `zeff help W0205` explains a code

## bare_name
error[Z0101]: nothing is called `skipped` here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:17
  |
1 | warn("x", code: skipped)
  |                 ^^^^^^^ not a binding

## note_bound
warning[W0101]: `n` hides the function `data::n`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:5
  |
1 | let n = note("x")
  |     ^ a binding with a built-in name
  |
  = help: the function is still reachable as `data::n`; a different name avoids the confusion
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be bound
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let n = note("x")
  |         ^^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: `print` and the other statements that print or warn return nothing; use the value they were given

## name_of_text
error[Z0401]: `v` of `name_of` must be a Var, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | name_of("educ")
  |         ^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: name a variable of the frame, without quotes

## name_of_nothing
error[Z0406]: `name_of` needs `v`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | name_of()
  | ^^^^^^^ `v` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `name_of(v)`
